Original commit body from c134611cb5e632f0f0f300618f0274e656f2f7e0:

packages/htrac-frontend was a two-commit (2026-04-04) Lit + Vite scaffold:
812 lines that imported no BlockSuite despite the package's name, were
never built or tested in CI, never reached a wheel, and were unreachable
from any command (run_server() builds the app without a static_dir or a
TrackerSet). Its only external effect was the repository's Dependabot
banner -- 44 of the 47 alerts came from its lockfile (WI-popal).

The decision it rested on has changed: BlockSuite's standalone npm line
has published nothing substantive since 0.22.4 (2025-07-01) and its repo
carries only bot PRs since 2025-07-07, so ADR-0019's "learning vehicle"
rationale no longer has an object. Owner ruling 2026-10-16 (WI-pupod):
the frontend is re-scoped to a Yjs-backed tracker document with BlockNote
and @xyflow/react views (ADR-0062 / WI-tofog and dependents), and the
scaffold is removed rather than its lockfile bumped -- a fix that would
have aged straight back into alerts. When that work starts it begins from
a React scaffold; this one stays recoverable from history.

ADR-0019's status line claimed the BlockSuite web frontend was
"implemented and shipped in v0.2.0"; it now says what exists. The frontend
row, the rationale paragraph, the Part A frontend bullet and open question
§"Web frontend framework choice" are rewritten to the new decision per the
ADR lifecycle rule (excise, don't banner); the index row follows. Stray
references removed: the mypy exclude in pyproject.toml, check-mypy-ratchet's
special case, and a comment in linkers/websocket.py that cited the deleted
TS client as its example.

